# Ralph Tasks

## Project
- Goal: Add priority levels to tasks with filtering and editing capabilities
- Repo: https://github.com/example/myapp
- Branch: ralph/task-priority
- Status: PLANNING_PENDING
- Updated: 2026-01-30

## Task List
> Created by `./ralph.sh plan` using Oracle. Each task is independently completable.
> After planning, status changes to IMPLEMENTING and workers execute tasks.
> Tasks with dependencies will be skipped until their dependencies are complete.

(Run `./ralph.sh plan` to generate tasks from the goal above)

---

## Task Format Reference

Each task follows this structure:

```markdown
### T001 - <short title>
- Status: [ ] TODO
- Priority: P1
- Depends: 
- Outcome: <one line describing expected result>
- Context:
  - `path/to/relevant/file.ts`
- Checks:
  - `npm run typecheck`
  - `npm test`
- Notes:
  - (written by worker after completion)
```

### Dependency Examples

```markdown
### T001 - Create database schema
- Status: [ ] TODO
- Priority: P1
- Depends: 
- Outcome: Priority column added to tasks table

### T002 - Add API endpoint
- Status: [ ] TODO
- Priority: P1
- Depends: T001
- Outcome: GET /api/tasks returns priority field

### T003 - Create UI component
- Status: [ ] TODO
- Priority: P2
- Depends: T001, T002
- Outcome: PriorityBadge renders correctly
```

In this example:
- T001 has no dependencies and will be selected first
- T002 depends on T001, so it won't start until T001 is marked `[x]`
- T003 depends on both T001 and T002, so it waits for both
